# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Allowlist .gitignore
#
# This file ignores EVERYTHING and then un-ignores only what is meant to be
# published. A new scratch file, backup folder or stray copy dropped into this
# directory is therefore invisible to git by default — it can never be swept
# into a commit by `git add -A`.
#
# To publish something new you must add a line for it here. That is the point.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Everything at the root is ignored, then named files are restored ─────────
/*

!/.gitignore
!/.env.example
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/LICENSE
!/requirements.txt
!/push_to_github.sh
!/Labs/
!/Slides/
!/pdf/
!/skills/

# ── Labs/ — the notebooks, the two index documents, the generators ───────────
Labs/*
!Labs/[01][0-9]_*.ipynb
!Labs/README_Lab_Index.md
!Labs/SESSION_FINDINGS_2026-08.md
!Labs/cost_meter.py
!Labs/build/

Labs/build/*
!Labs/build/*.py

# ── Slides/ — the deck index and the generators. The .pptx files are NOT
#    published: 21 MB of binaries would bloat the history and they rebuild from
#    the generators. pdf/ carries the readable copy. Attach .pptx to a Release.
Slides/*
!Slides/README_Deck_Index.md
!Slides/build/

Slides/build/*
!Slides/build/*.js
!Slides/build/package.json
!Slides/build/assets/

Slides/build/assets/*
!Slides/build/assets/logo.png

# ── pdf/ — one PDF per deck, numbered. Nothing else. ─────────────────────────
pdf/*
!pdf/[01][0-9]_*.pdf

# ── skills/ — the Agent Skill files and their README ─────────────────────────
skills/*
!skills/*.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt and braces. The rules above already exclude all of these, but naming
# them documents the intent and protects against a future negation that is
# broader than it looks.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Secrets — never, under any circumstances
.env
*.env
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# macOS, editors, Python, Jupyter
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/
node_modules/

# Office lock files — the `~$Deck.pptx` stubs Word/PowerPoint leaves behind
~$*

# Working material that lives here but is not published
Labs_v2/
_backup_*/
*.bundle
* copy.*
*copy.pptx
*copy.md

# Lab-generated artefacts — regenerated on every run
Labs/data/
Labs/out/
Labs/skills/
Labs/context7_mcp_config.json

# NOTE: Labs/cost_meter.py IS published (un-ignored above). Lab 00 writes it,
# but shipping a copy means a reader who opens Lab 05 first still has a working
# meter. The committed copy is byte-identical to what Lab 00 emits, so re-running
# Lab 00 produces no diff. If you change the rates, change them in
# Labs/build/gen_a.py and re-run Lab 00, then commit both.
